---
import ZoneDiagram from './ZoneDiagram.astro';
---

<section id="how" class="section" aria-labelledby="how-title">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="section-head section-head--center">
      <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
      <h2 id="how-title">Three steps, then it stays out of the way</h2>
      <p class="lead">Set up your zones once. After that, snapping is a drag and a key you already know.</p>
    </header>

    <ol class="steps">
      <li class="card step">
        <ZoneDiagram variant="editor" />
        <div class="body">
          <p class="num" aria-hidden="true">1</p>
          <h3>Define your zones</h3>
          <p>
            Open the layout editor on any monitor. Split zones, drag the dividers, or start from a template: halves,
            thirds, a 2&times;2 grid, columns or a priority grid.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="card step">
        <ZoneDiagram variant="drag" />
        <div class="body">
          <p class="num" aria-hidden="true">2</p>
          <h3>Hold Shift and drag</h3>
          <p>
            Start dragging a window and hold <kbd>Shift</kbd> (or the key you choose). The zones of the monitor under
            your cursor appear, and the one you are over lights up.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="card step">
        <ZoneDiagram variant="snap" />
        <div class="body">
          <p class="num" aria-hidden="true">3</p>
          <h3>Release to snap</h3>
          <p>
            Let go of the mouse and the window moves to fit that zone. Changed your mind? Release
            <kbd>Shift</kbd> before the mouse button and nothing moves.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .steps {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-m);
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 18rem), 1fr));
  }

  .step {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-m);
    padding: var(--space-m);
  }

  .body {
    position: relative;
    padding-top: var(--space-2xs);
  }

  .num {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 2rem;
    height: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-accent);
    color: var(--color-on-accent);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xs);
  }

  .body p:last-child {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
</style>
